{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>להשקיט לו מימי רע</b> — harsh decrees issuing from the heavens, as in the manner of עושה שלום ובורא רע (Isaiah 45:7), and the opposite of this applies to the wicked, for HaShem prolongs his days until his day comes, the time of his punishment. And because the expression יכרה לשון is under a masculine form, the correct reading is להיות שחת, from the root השחתה. And the tav is a root letter, or it is after the manner of ודעת לנפשך ינעם ולא יבצר ממך מזמה (Proverbs 24:4). And it would be שחת, like שוחד, and העד יכרה."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 94, :notes {0 "The comment addresses a grammatical difficulty in the psalm: the verb form יכרה is parsed as masculine against its apparent feminine subject לשון. Ibn Ezra resolves this by reading שחת (a masculine noun) as the subject and taking כרה in the sense of 'dig' as in שוחד/bribery."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:16.772017572Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}